    <!-- 
    
        Displayed ratings can be one of the following:
        
        1.  Display an entire rating system as defined in the <ratingsettings> section above:
        
            <displayedratingsystem ratingsystemid="" />

        2.  Group multiple rating systems together into one logical display, overriding some or all names.
            In this case the ratingsystemid from the <displayedratingsystem> element, and the ratingid
            from the <displayedrating> element are used to look up the display string for that rating
            from the list above.  In this case the <displayedratingsystem> element can contain a
            description attribute which overrides the description on the rating system above.  Currently
            the <displayedrating> element CANNOT contain a description attribute.  The <mappedrating>
            elements indicate what is actually saved to the XLAST file when the <displayedrating> is
            selected by the user.
            
        !!!! NOTE !!!! This section MUST occur after the <ratingsettings> element.
        
    -->

